wing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brcontainer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brcontainer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brcontainer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brcontainer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brcontainer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brcontainer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brcontainer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brcontainer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-21T16:02:20Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T16:09:24Z","body":"# System information\n\n- Godot v4.6.rc2\n- Windows 10 (build 19045)\n- Multi-window, 1 monitor\n- Vulkan (Forward+)\n- NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 6GB Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8157)\n- 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13420H (12 threads)\n- 31.69 GiB memory\n\n# Empty scene\n\n* D3D12\n    * GPU Time: 2.17ms\n    * FPS: 459\n\n* Vulkan\n    * GPU Time: 0.65ms\n    * FPS: 1515\n\n| D3D12 | VULKAN |\n| --- | --- |\n| <img width=\"1920\" height=\"1017\" alt=\"D3D12\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7f7ab164-07a7-4df6-a977-5c716abdde98\" /> |  <img width=\"1920\" height=\"1017\" alt=\"VULKAN\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5c107f75-9bf0-4066-a307-c2d345431f89\" /> |\n\n# Empty scene with default env\n\n* D3D12\n    * GPU Time: 3.69ms\n    * FPS: 270\n\n* Vulkan\n    * GPU Time: 2.82ms\n    * FPS: 354\n\n| D3D12 | VULKAN |\n| --- | --- |\n| <img width=\"1920\" height=\"1017\" alt=\"D3D12 + env\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aad2e082-f630-4f0c-a18c-c47d0bb13d34\" /> | <img width=\"1920\" height=\"1017\" alt=\"VULKAN + env\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a63ed4e8-ea3c-4839-a517-123595012cd6\" /> |\n\n> Note: FPS can take a moment to stabilize while the cursor is over the scene viewport. Additionally, since the editor typically runs in windowed mode with multiple panels, focusing other windows can lead to noticeable variations in FPS and GPU time. This is expected behavior.\n\n# An exported project with a simple scene:\n\nThe test was performed using \"Exclusive Fullscreen\":\n\n* D3D12: FPS: 701\n* Vulkan: FPS: 677\n\n> Note: The only detail I observed is that D3D12 appears to take a bit longer to stabilize, though the difference is not significant.\n\n| D3D12 | VULKAN |\n| --- | --- |\n<img width=\"800\" height=\"600\" alt=\"D3D12\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/140359e5-a428-43b5-9ce4-9863d0819efc\" /> | <img width=\"800\" height=\"600\" alt=\"VULKAN\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8cc5591a-dbfb-4cbd-8166-b8c51e141c18\" />\n\n# MRP\n\n[new_4.6.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24771296/new_4.6.zip)\n\nThe pck and override.cfg files are already present in the build directory, making testing easier.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3779169977/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]